Hello!

You should use s3 driver, s3virge driver is for S3 Virge, not S3 Trio.
Xorg -configure will create automagically a file for your needs.
If it doesn't work with that file, then it is either a bug in the =20
driver, or an unsupported card (strange, but could be)

> The other issue, about the text console going dead during boot,
> though, seems to be something else. I had this machine running =20
> without using the graphics at all. When I first set it up, I didn't =20
> have a keyboard and monitor handy for it, so I installed it to use =20
> the serial port as a console. I think what must be happening is that =20
> the console gets switched to the serial port at just that point, and =20
> of course I've disconnected the other terminal from that port. So I =20
> need to figure out how to change that. In some distributions it would =20
> mean compiling or at least loading a new kernel. I'm not sure in =20
> Debian though whether I have to do that or just change a =20
> configuration option somewhere. Slackware would let me replace the =20
> kernel alone from the installation CD, for instance. But when I tried =20
> that with Debian it wanted to repartition the drive and reinstall =20
> everything. Obviously that's not my goal, I have the system all set =20
> up and customized now.

Of course it doesn't need niether a kernel recompinling nor a setup =20
from install CD.
You only have to delete the console redirection setting in aboot.conf, =20
simply delete a setting like "console=3DttyS1,115200" from the kernel =20
line.

Bye
gl



