On Sun, Nov 18, 2007 at 02:35:24PM +0100, Emmanuel PERRIN wrote:
> I have a PWS 500a on which NT works "perfectly". I try to use linux on
> it (instead of windows). I succed in installing milo (v1.5) but none of
> the kernels I have found boot up. Is it a wrong milo version ?

Switch the firmware to unix mode (in advanced settings, which is F6 on
one of the menus).  The PWS in SRM mode boots perfectly and runs just
fine.

I haven't managed to make milo work on anything I have tried so far, and
due to a lack of source code no one can really fix it anymore.

Of course that means you can't run NT on it (as if that is a loss).

--
Len Sorensen



